## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates understanding of consent-driven data minimization, offline safety, and the relationship between consent lifecycle and CCA score calculation.

## Key Concepts
- Consent tokens gate data exposure
- policy_version controls exposure granularity
- Idempotent, offline-safe compute operations
- Per-user data retention settings

## Code Example
```javascript
async function computeCCA(userIdMasked, consentToken, policyVersion) {
  const consent = await consentStore.validate(consentToken, policyVersion);
  if (!consent?.allowed) {
    throw new Error('Not authorized');
  }
  const score = await calculateScore(userIdMasked, consent);
  return { user_id_masked: userIdMasked, cca_score: score };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests API design discipline, latency considerations, and privacy handling for a live scoring service. It requires concrete endpoints, data fields, and rollout strategies rather than abstract concepts.

## Key Concepts
- Deterministic scoring with consistent model behavior across regions
- Privacy-first design with masked user identifiers
- Canary rollout and backpressure mechanisms for safe deployment
- Observability: latency tracking, error monitoring, drift detection

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeScore(features, salt) {
  let h = 0;
  for(const f of features) {
    h = ((h << 5) - h) + f.charCodeAt(0);
    h = h & h;
  }
  return Math.abs(h + salt) % 1000;
}
```

